<title>USA: University of Ill. repriced, top yield 6.07 pct.</title>
<headline>University of Ill. repriced, top yield 6.07 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co. said Tuesday it repriced the Board of Trustees of the University of Illinois' $46.2 million bond deal, lowering yields in several maturities and raising the top yield in 2026 to 6.07 percent from 6.05 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:  </p>
<p>THE BOARD OF TRUSTEES OF THE</p>
<p>UNIVERSITY OF ILLINOIS</p>
<p>RE: $46,220,000*</p>
<p>HEALTH SERVICES FACILITIES SYSTEM REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>SERIES 1997A</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>THE ACCOUNT IS CLOSED.</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa - AMBAC     S&amp;P: AAA - AMBAC</p>
<p>		 A3 UNDERLYING	  AA- UNDERLYING</p>
<p>    DATED: 04/15/1997	  FIRST COUPON: 10/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 10/01</p>
